  "result": "That decision is made in `src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts`:\n\n- **`prefersMetaKey(platform)`** works out what \"mod\" means. If the platform string matches `mac|iphone|ipad|ipod`, \"mod\" means Meta (Command); on anything else it means Control.\n- **`matchesShortcut(keys, event, platform)`** first calls `parseShortcut` to split the shortcut into its modifier keys and main key. It then checks that the pressed key matches, turns \"mod\" into Ctrl or Meta using `prefersMetaKey`, and requires the event's `ctrlKey`, `metaKey`, `altKey` and `shiftKey` to match exactly.\n\n`src/hooks/use-keyboard-shortcut.ts` only listens for the keydown, passes in `navigator.platform` and calls `matchesShortcut`, so the matching logic itself lives in `shortcut-match.ts`.\n\nANSWER: src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts",
